<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Portfolio.py::chunk:461> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 461 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "function" ;
    rf:content """def frc_optimization(
        self, model="Classic", obj="Sharpe", kelly=None, rf=0, l=2, hist=True
    ):
        r\"\"\"
        This method that calculates the risk parity portfolio using the risk
        budgeting approach :cite:`a-Cajas13` according to the objective function
        selected by the user. The general problem that solves is:

        .. math::
            \\begin{aligned}
            \\underset{w_f}{\\text{optimize}} & \\quad F(w)\\\\
            \\text{s.t.} \\quad & \\quad \\begin{bmatrix} W_{F}  & w_{F} \\\\ w^{\\prime}_{F} & 1 \\end{bmatrix} \\succeq 0 \\\\
            & \\quad A w \\leq b \\\\
            & \\quad w = (B^{\\prime})^{+} w_{F} \\\\
            & \\quad A_{\\text{FRC}} \\text{diag}\\left ( \\bar{\\Sigma} W_{F} \\right) \\leq b_{\\text{FRC}} \\, \\text{Tr} \\left ( \\bar{\\Sigma} W_{F} \\right ) \\\\
            & \\quad W_{F} \\in \\mathbf{S}^{m}\\\\
            \\end{aligned}

        Where:

        :math:`w_f` are the weights of the risk factors.

        :math:`W_f`: is the symmetric matrix va""" ;
    rf:content_hash "ca7de67059f32f3473054d04d0f4bf8a600b6bb424efaeb6b380043ff33cd565" ;
    rf:line_end 4889 ;
    rf:line_start 4863 ;
    rf:relative_path "Portfolio.py" ;
    rf:section "frc_optimization" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/riskfolio/src/Portfolio.py" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Portfolio.py::chunk:462> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 462 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "function" ;
    rf:content """:math:`w_f` are the weights of the risk factors.

        :math:`W_f`: is the symmetric matrix variable that approximates :math:`w_f w^{\\prime}_f`.

        :math:`B` is the loadings matrix.

        :math:`Aw \\leq b`: is a set of linear constraints on asset weights.

        :math:`\\bar{\\Sigma} = \\left ((B^{\\prime})^{+} \\right )^{\\prime} \\Sigma (B^{\\prime})^{+}`.

        :math:`A_{\\text{FRC}} \\text{diag}\\left ( \\bar{\\Sigma} W_{F} \\right) \\leq b_{\\text{FRC}} \\, \\text{Tr} \\left ( \\bar{\\Sigma} W_{F} \\right )`: is a set of linear factor risk contribution constraints.

        Parameters
        ----------
        model : str can be 'Classic' or 'FM'
            The model used for optimize the portfolio.
            The default is 'Classic'. Possible values are:

            - 'Classic': uses estimates of expected return vector and covariance matrix that depends on historical data.
            - 'FM': uses estimates of expected return vector and covariance matrix based on a Risk Factor""" ;
    rf:content_hash "b27da3bb285eb429eee85d7f99e57e53212453e7d6b054f1615703b54126ff75" ;
    rf:line_end 4913 ;
    rf:line_start 4886 ;
    rf:relative_path "Portfolio.py" ;
    rf:section "frc_optimization" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/riskfolio/src/Portfolio.py" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Portfolio.py::chunk:463> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 463 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "function" ;
    rf:content """- 'FM': uses estimates of expected return vector and covariance matrix based on a Risk Factor model specified by the user.

        obj : str can be {'MinRisk', 'Utility', 'Sharpe' or 'MaxRet'}.
            Objective function of the optimization model.
            The default is 'Sharpe'. Possible values are:

            - 'MinRisk': Minimize the selected risk measure.
            - 'Utility': Maximize the Utility function :math:`\\mu w - l \\phi_{i}(w)`.
            - 'Sharpe': Maximize the risk adjusted return ratio based on the selected risk measure.
            - 'MaxRet': Maximize the expected return of the portfolio.

        kelly : str, optional
            Method used to calculate mean return. Possible values are: None for
            arithmetic mean return, "approx" for approximate mean logarithmic
            return using first and second moment and "exact" for mean logarithmic
            return. The default is None.
        rf : float, optional
            Risk free""" ;
    rf:content_hash "78609a33a271b64b2f296a4b0a55aeb61d30623a0061c2933ecfe48735d4a306" ;
    rf:line_end 4937 ;
    rf:line_start 4910 ;
    rf:relative_path "Portfolio.py" ;
    rf:section "frc_optimization" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/riskfolio/src/Portfolio.py" .

