<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/RiskFunctions.py::chunk:75> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 75 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "function" ;
    rf:content """def Sharpe(
    returns,
    w=None,
    mu=None,
    cov=None,
    rm="MV",
    rf=0,
    alpha=0.05,
    a_sim=100,
    beta=None,
    b_sim=None,
    kappa=0.3,
    kappa_g=None,
    solver="CLARABEL",
):
    r\"\"\"
    Calculate the Risk Adjusted Return Ratio from a portfolio returns series.

    .. math::
        \\text{Sharpe}(X) =  \\frac{\\mathbb{E}(X) -
        r_{f}}{\\phi(X)}

    Where:

    :math:`X` is the vector of portfolio returns.

    :math:`r_{f}` is the risk free rate, when the risk measure is

    :math:`\\text{LPM}` uses instead of :math:`r_{f}` the :math:`\\text{MAR}`.

    :math:`\\phi(X)` is a convex risk measure. The risk measures availabe are:

    Parameters
    ----------

    returns : DataFrame or nd-array of shape (n_samples, n_features)
        Features matrix, where n_samples is the number of samples and
        n_features is the number of features.
    w : DataFrame or 1d-array of shape (n_assets, 1)
        Weights matrix, where n_assets is the number of ass""" ;
    rf:content_hash "7046d0638fce93910ab3cb1a5bbb3fbd31c8f177ed527ca5489cbd3bb0a84f92" ;
    rf:line_end 2164 ;
    rf:line_start 2137 ;
    rf:relative_path "RiskFunctions.py" ;
    rf:section "Sharpe" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/riskfolio/src/RiskFunctions.py" .

