<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2010%20-%20Risk%20Parity%20Portfolio%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:10> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 10 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content """## 3. Estimating Risk Parity Portfolios for Other Risk Measures

In this part I will calculate risk parity portfolios. First I'm going to calculate risk parity portfolio when we use variance as risk measure, then I'm going to calculate the risk parity portfolios for all available risk measures.

### 3.1 Calculating the risk parity portfolio for variance.""" ;
    rf:content_hash "5b550bfe40b0e520b5d993f5df3ded96688e9911cab6f075e2baa020155508b7" ;
    rf:line_end 10 ;
    rf:line_start 10 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 10 - Risk Parity Portfolio Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 10 - Risk Parity Portfolio Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2010%20-%20Risk%20Parity%20Portfolio%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:11> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 11 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """b = None # Risk contribution constraints vector

w_rp = port.rp_optimization(model=model, rm=rm, rf=rf, b=b, hist=hist)

display(w.T)""" ;
    rf:content_hash "7ccb16032d3ccb0730d01275770d25030852597cc5d9d223c749a010f0a8e653" ;
    rf:line_end 11 ;
    rf:line_start 11 ;
