<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2012%20-%20Worst%20Case%20Mean%20Variance%20Portfolio%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:10> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 10 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content """## 3. Estimating Worst Case Mean Variance Portfolios with Box Uncertainty Sets based on Bootstrapping.

### 3.1 Calculating the worst case mean variance portfolio.

I'm going to use box uncertainty sets and the parameters of this sets are going to be estimated through block bootstrapping. This means that the limits of uncertainty sets are based on percentiles.""" ;
    rf:content_hash "97d509ae7c3140198d8a3257966b285143e763b0bf859ef900366963f085230f" ;
    rf:line_end 10 ;
    rf:line_start 10 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 12 - Worst Case Mean Variance Portfolio Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 12 - Worst Case Mean Variance Portfolio Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2012%20-%20Worst%20Case%20Mean%20Variance%20Portfolio%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:11> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 11 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """\"\"\"
self.cov_l = cov_l
self.cov_u = cov_u
self.cov_mu = cov_mu
self.cov_sigma = cov_sigma
self.d_mu = d_mu
self.k_mu = k_mu
self.k_sigma = k_sigma
\"\"\"

print(port.cov_l)""" ;
    rf:content_hash "99a7cd0a88798408625381a3defe0924ea8d8c26aa1bab25b621a9ccddd61e86" ;
    rf:line_end 11 ;
    rf:line_start 11 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 12 - Worst Case Mean Variance Portfolio Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_cell" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 12 - Worst Case Mean Variance Portfolio Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2012%20-%20Worst%20Case%20Mean%20Variance%20Portfolio%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:12> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 12 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """# Select method and estimate worst case input parameters:

box = 's' # Method to estimate box uncertainty sets parameters
ellip = 's' # Method to estimate elliptical uncertainty sets parameters
q = 0.05 # Confidence level for bootstrapping and k ellipsoidal uncertainty sets constraints
n_sim = 3000 # Number of scenarios for bootstrapping
window = 3 # Size of each block for block bootstrapping
dmu = 0.1 # delta to increase or decrease the mean vector
dcov = 0.1 # delta to increase or decrease the covariance matrix
seed = 0 

port.wc_stats(box=box, ellip=ellip, q=q, n_sim=n_sim, window=window, dmu=dmu, dcov=dcov, seed=seed)

# Estimate worst case optimal portfolio using selected uncertainty sets:
# port.solvers = ['CLARABEL']

Umu = 'box' # Type of uncertainty set for mean vector
Ucov = 'box' # Type of uncertaity set for covariance matrix

w_wc_1 = port.wc_optimization(obj=obj, rf=rf, l=l, Umu=Umu, Ucov=Ucov)

display(w_wc_1.T)""" ;
    rf:content_hash "273f9958f171df97d92509b81c8496773b357483c76443c848eaf5d4bde6aed3" ;
    rf:line_end 12 ;
    rf:line_start 12 ;
