<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2015%20-%20Mean%20Entropic%20Value%20at%20Risk%20(EVaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:14> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 14 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content """## 3. Estimating Risk Parity Portfolios for EVaR

### 3.1 Calculating the risk parity portfolio for EVaR.

The risk parity portfolio for the EVaR risk measure is the solution of the problem:

$$
\\begin{aligned}
& \\min_{w,\\, z} & & \\text{EVaR}_{\\alpha}(r w) - b \\ln(w)\\\\
& & & 1^{T}w = 0 \\\\
& & & w \\geq 0 \\\\
\\end{aligned}
$$

Where $w$ are the weights of assets, $b$ is the vector of constraints, by default is a vector of 1/(number of assets).""" ;
    rf:content_hash "fe1b1873d643d676dd566de89ba6b35dfd0649eaebcdecbf142fecddf06632cd" ;
    rf:line_end 12 ;
    rf:line_start 12 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 15 - Mean Entropic Value at Risk (EVaR) Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 15 - Mean Entropic Value at Risk (EVaR) Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2015%20-%20Mean%20Entropic%20Value%20at%20Risk%20(EVaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:15> a rf:Chunk ;
