<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%202%20-%20Portfolio%20Optimization%20using%20Risk%20Factors%20and%20Stepwise%20Regression.ipynb::chunk:30> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 30 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content """## 4. Estimating Portfolios Using Risk Factors with Other Risk Measures

In this part I will calculate optimal portfolios for several risk measures. I will find the portfolios that maximize the risk adjusted return for all available risk measures.

### 4.1 Calculate Optimal Portfolios for Several Risk Measures.

I will mantain the constraints on risk factors.""" ;
    rf:content_hash "f1cfe22c5e8a7593e132ad3d32bfed0c420afe45cb90aec805185e84b23022fd" ;
    rf:line_end 30 ;
    rf:line_start 30 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 2 - Portfolio Optimization using Risk Factors and Stepwise Regression.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 2 - Portfolio Optimization using Risk Factors and Stepwise Regression.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%202%20-%20Portfolio%20Optimization%20using%20Risk%20Factors%20and%20Stepwise%20Regression.ipynb::chunk:31> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 31 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """# Risk Measures available:
#
# 'MV': Standard Deviation.
# 'MAD': Mean Absolute Deviation.
# 'MSV': Semi Standard Deviation.
# 'FLPM': First Lower Partial Moment (Omega Ratio).
# 'SLPM': Second Lower Partial Moment (Sortino Ratio).
# 'CVaR': Conditional Value at Risk.
# 'EVaR': Entropic Value at Risk.
# 'WR': Worst Realization (Minimax)
# 'MDD': Maximum Drawdown of uncompounded cumulative returns (Calmar Ratio).
# 'ADD': Average Drawdown of uncompounded cumulative returns.
# 'CDaR': Conditional Drawdown at Risk of uncompounded cumulative returns.
# 'EDaR': Entropic Drawdown at Risk of uncompounded cumulative returns.
# 'UCI': Ulcer Index of uncompounded cumulative returns.

# port.reset_linear_constraints() # To reset linear constraints (factor constraints)

rms = ['MV', 'MAD', 'MSV', 'FLPM', 'SLPM', 'CVaR',
       'EVaR', 'WR', 'MDD', 'ADD', 'CDaR', 'UCI', 'EDaR']

w_s = pd.DataFrame([])

# When we use hist = True the risk measures all calculated
# using historical returns, while when""" ;
    rf:content_hash "7cea3ebd343ab14c1594bd435da40c361e554718d1e3e70974fdc9744346fadc" ;
    rf:line_end 31 ;
    rf:line_start 31 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 2 - Portfolio Optimization using Risk Factors and Stepwise Regression.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_cell" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 2 - Portfolio Optimization using Risk Factors and Stepwise Regression.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%202%20-%20Portfolio%20Optimization%20using%20Risk%20Factors%20and%20Stepwise%20Regression.ipynb::chunk:32> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 32 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """)

# When we use hist = True the risk measures all calculated
# using historical returns, while when hist = False the
# risk measures are calculated using the expected returns 
#  based on risk factor model: R = a + B * F

hist = False
for i in rms:
    w = port.optimization(model=model, rm=i, obj=obj, rf=rf, l=l, hist=hist)
    w_s = pd.concat([w_s, w], axis=1)
    
w_s.columns = rms""" ;
    rf:content_hash "ffe40cf9989586239396afc8b2911313d24855963a22097af3495f90994923ce" ;
    rf:line_end 31 ;
    rf:line_start 31 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 2 - Portfolio Optimization using Risk Factors and Stepwise Regression.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_cell" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 2 - Portfolio Optimization using Risk Factors and Stepwise Regression.ipynb" .

