<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2029%20-%20Hierarchical%20Risk%20Parity%20(HRP)%20Portfolio%20Optimization%20with%20Constraints.ipynb::chunk:4> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 4 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """import riskfolio as rp

# Plotting Assets Clusters

ax = rp.plot_dendrogram(returns=Y,
                        codependence='pearson',
                        linkage='single',
                        k=None,
                        max_k=10,
                        leaf_order=True,
                        ax=None)""" ;
    rf:content_hash "7e2afd492feb38603dd29d65290b568808fa7f0fbe85bd6f92b149b1138e7b9f" ;
    rf:line_end 4 ;
    rf:line_start 4 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 29 - Hierarchical Risk Parity (HRP) Portfolio Optimization with Constraints.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_cell" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 29 - Hierarchical Risk Parity (HRP) Portfolio Optimization with Constraints.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2029%20-%20Hierarchical%20Risk%20Parity%20(HRP)%20Portfolio%20Optimization%20with%20Constraints.ipynb::chunk:5> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 5 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content """The dendrogram above suggest that optimal number of clusters are four. However HRP portfolios don't use a number of clusters as input.

## 2. Estimating HRP Portfolio

This is the original model proposed by López de Prado (2016). Riskfolio-Lib expand this model to 32 risk measures.

### 2.1 Calculating the HRP portfolio""" ;
    rf:content_hash "f7b205a9c44367b542df9211afb4b92e9ccca508ba6f20477dafedacc0b62a3e" ;
    rf:line_end 5 ;
    rf:line_start 5 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 29 - Hierarchical Risk Parity (HRP) Portfolio Optimization with Constraints.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 29 - Hierarchical Risk Parity (HRP) Portfolio Optimization with Constraints.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2029%20-%20Hierarchical%20Risk%20Parity%20(HRP)%20Portfolio%20Optimization%20with%20Constraints.ipynb::chunk:6> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 6 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """# Building the portfolio object
port = rp.HCPortfolio(returns=Y)

# Estimate optimal portfolio:

model = 'HRP' # Could be HRP or HERC
codependence = 'pearson' # Correlation matrix used to group assets in clusters
rm = 'MV' # Risk measure used, this time will be variance
rf = 0 # Risk free rate
linkage = 'single' # Linkage method used to build clusters
max_k = 10 # Max number of clusters used in two difference gap statistic, only for HERC model
leaf_order = True # Consider optimal order of leafs in dendrogram

w = port.optimization(model=model,
                      codependence=codependence,
                      rm=rm,
                      rf=rf,
                      linkage=linkage,
                      max_k=max_k,
                      leaf_order=leaf_order)

display(w.T)""" ;
    rf:content_hash "c8a11124040cca811c7280a454c25d18956c6d177c46ea57ccaeb1f58d0d805b" ;
    rf:line_end 6 ;
    rf:line_start 6 ;
