<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2036%20-%20Mean%20Tail%20Gini%20Range%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:4> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 4 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content """## 2. Estimating Mean Tail Gini Range Portfolios

The Tail Gini Range is an specific case of the OWA portfolio model proposed by __[Cajas (2021)](https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=3988927)__ . 

It is recommended to use MOSEK to optimize Tail Gini Range, due to it requires more computing power for the number of constraints and variables the model use.

Instructions to install MOSEK are in this __[link](https://docs.mosek.com/9.2/install/installation.html)__, is better to install using Anaconda. Also you will need a license, I recommend you that ask for an academic license __[here](https://www.mosek.com/products/academic-licenses/)__.

### 2.1 Calculating the portfolio that optimize return/Tail Gini Range ratio.""" ;
    rf:content_hash "ed4c626bfae5d29176c737a4fc3d39c220e47b63203ffd94a88774c4d42ea077" ;
    rf:line_end 4 ;
    rf:line_start 4 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 36 - Mean Tail Gini Range Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 36 - Mean Tail Gini Range Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2036%20-%20Mean%20Tail%20Gini%20Range%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:5> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 5 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """import riskfolio as rp
import mosek

# Building the portfolio object
port = rp.Portfolio(returns=Y)

# Calculating optimum portfolio

# Select method and estimate input parameters:

method_mu='hist' # Method to estimate expected returns based on historical data.
method_cov='hist' # Method to estimate covariance matrix based on historical data.

port.assets_stats(method_mu=method_mu, method_cov=method_cov)

# Estimate optimal portfolio:

port.solvers = ['MOSEK'] # It is recommended to use mosek when optimizing GMD
port.sol_params = {'MOSEK': {'mosek_params': {mosek.iparam.num_threads: 2}}}

port.alpha = 0.05
port.beta = 0.05
model ='Classic' # Could be Classic (historical), BL (Black Litterman) or FM (Factor Model)
rm = 'TGRG' # Risk measure used, this time will be Tail Gini Range
obj = 'Sharpe' # Objective function, could be MinRisk, MaxRet, Utility or Sharpe
hist = True # Use historical scenarios for risk measures that depend on scenarios
rf = 0 # Risk free rate
l = 0 # Risk aversion""" ;
    rf:content_hash "7327fb918efd5fbbfccf8482375f3bbbea81b12b62a9bb1832c80f4f70a7a355" ;
    rf:line_end 5 ;
    rf:line_start 5 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 36 - Mean Tail Gini Range Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_cell" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 36 - Mean Tail Gini Range Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2036%20-%20Mean%20Tail%20Gini%20Range%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:6> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 6 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """scenarios for risk measures that depend on scenarios
