<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2040%20-%20Mean%20Relativistic%20Value%20at%20Risk%20(RLVaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:4> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 4 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content """## 2. Estimating Mean Relativistic Value at Risk (RLVaR) Portfolios

The Relativistic Value at Risk (RLVaR) portfolio model proposed by __[Cajas (2023)](https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4378498)__ shows how to optimize the RLVaR of portfolio returns in a similar way than portfolio Entropic Value at Risk (EVaR). The RLVaR is a coherent risk measure that is a generalization of EVaR based on Kaniadakis entropy.

It is recommended to use MOSEK to optimize RLVaR due to RLVaR model use the power cone.

Instructions to install MOSEK are in this __[link](https://docs.mosek.com/9.2/install/installation.html)__, is better to install using Anaconda. Also you will need a license, I recommend you that ask for an academic license __[here](https://www.mosek.com/products/academic-licenses/)__.

### 2.1 Calculating the portfolio that optimize return/RLVaR ratio.""" ;
    rf:content_hash "5fa9ac78187fff871c71f1389a1580216b0ee59ee91c90c89aa8bb3e744762a4" ;
    rf:line_end 4 ;
    rf:line_start 4 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 40 - Mean Relativistic Value at Risk (RLVaR) Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 40 - Mean Relativistic Value at Risk (RLVaR) Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2040%20-%20Mean%20Relativistic%20Value%20at%20Risk%20(RLVaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:5> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 5 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """import riskfolio as rp
import mosek

# Building the portfolio object
port = rp.Portfolio(returns=Y)

# Calculating optimum portfolio

# Select method and estimate input parameters:

method_mu='hist' # Method to estimate expected returns based on historical data.
method_cov='hist' # Method to estimate covariance matrix based on historical data.

port.assets_stats(method_mu=method_mu,
                  method_cov=method_cov,
                  )

# Estimate optimal portfolio:

port.solvers = ['MOSEK'] # It is recommended to use mosek when optimizing GMD
port.sol_params = {'MOSEK': {'mosek_params': {mosek.iparam.num_threads: 2}}}

kappa = 0.3
alpha = 0.05
port.kappa = kappa
port.alpha = alpha

model ='Classic' # Could be Classic (historical), BL (Black Litterman) or FM (Factor Model)
rm = 'RLVaR' # Risk measure used, this time will be Tail Gini Range
obj = 'Sharpe' # Objective function, could be MinRisk, MaxRet, Utility or Sharpe
hist = True # Use historical scenarios for risk measures tha""" ;
    rf:content_hash "91222e7126ddab6f212a2a4ad50d0be8feabe906bf7ca4464646d2734e29f969" ;
    rf:line_end 5 ;
    rf:line_start 5 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 40 - Mean Relativistic Value at Risk (RLVaR) Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_cell" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 40 - Mean Relativistic Value at Risk (RLVaR) Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2040%20-%20Mean%20Relativistic%20Value%20at%20Risk%20(RLVaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:6> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 6 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """d be MinRisk, MaxRet, Utility or Sharpe
hist = True # Use historical scenarios for risk measures that depend on scenarios
rf = 0 # Risk free rate
l = 0 # Risk aversion factor, only useful when obj is 'Utility'

w = port.optimization(model=model, rm=rm, obj=obj, rf=rf, l=l, hist=hist)

display(w.T)""" ;
    rf:content_hash "06192f41996664d10b04a7e64cef9b53cbd17acc763dd28b37da7b4093566a1a" ;
    rf:line_end 5 ;
    rf:line_start 5 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 40 - Mean Relativistic Value at Risk (RLVaR) Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_cell" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 40 - Mean Relativistic Value at Risk (RLVaR) Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2040%20-%20Mean%20Relativistic%20Value%20at%20Risk%20(RLVaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:7> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 7 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content "### 2.2 Plotting portfolio composition" ;
    rf:content_hash "139dad0e700529398da30487874450432ed6fa2daf80afd0fae10da2c09e2408" ;
    rf:line_end 6 ;
    rf:line_start 6 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 40 - Mean Relativistic Value at Risk (RLVaR) Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 40 - Mean Relativistic Value at Risk (RLVaR) Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2040%20-%20Mean%20Relativistic%20Value%20at%20Risk%20(RLVaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:8> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 8 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """# Plotting the composition of the portfolio

ax = rp.plot_pie(w=w,
                 title='Sharpe Mean - RLVaR',
                 others=0.05,
                 nrow=25,
                 cmap = "tab20",
                 height=6,
                 width=10,
