<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2041%20-%20Mean%20Relativistic%20Drawdown%20at%20Risk%20(RLDaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:3> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 3 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """# Calculating returns

Y = data[assets].iloc[-300:,:].pct_change().dropna()

display(Y.head())""" ;
    rf:content_hash "ed4a70513c7194cc8a2ee3e7aba878afdd542b99be75aa930c797489f36be8aa" ;
    rf:line_end 3 ;
    rf:line_start 3 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 41 - Mean Relativistic Drawdown at Risk (RLDaR) Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_cell" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 41 - Mean Relativistic Drawdown at Risk (RLDaR) Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2041%20-%20Mean%20Relativistic%20Drawdown%20at%20Risk%20(RLDaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:4> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 4 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content """## 2. Estimating Mean Relativistic Drawdown at Risk (RLDaR) Portfolios

The Relativistic Drawdown at Risk (RLDaR) portfolio model proposed by __[Cajas (2023)](https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4378498)__ shows how to optimize the RDVaR of portfolio returns in a similar way than portfolio Entropic Drawdown at Risk (EDaR). The RLDaR is a coherent risk measure that is a generalization of EDaR based on Kaniadakis entropy.

It is recommended to use MOSEK to optimize RLDaR due to RLDaR model use the power cone.

Instructions to install MOSEK are in this __[link](https://docs.mosek.com/9.2/install/installation.html)__, is better to install using Anaconda. Also you will need a license, I recommend you that ask for an academic license __[here](https://www.mosek.com/products/academic-licenses/)__.

### 2.1 Calculating the portfolio that optimize return/RLVaR ratio.""" ;
    rf:content_hash "f24e08cf4830de3818927884bae1152468ec8f9b70184331c5a6b881ca108d2b" ;
    rf:line_end 4 ;
    rf:line_start 4 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 41 - Mean Relativistic Drawdown at Risk (RLDaR) Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 41 - Mean Relativistic Drawdown at Risk (RLDaR) Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2041%20-%20Mean%20Relativistic%20Drawdown%20at%20Risk%20(RLDaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:5> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 5 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """import riskfolio as rp
import mosek

# Building the portfolio object
port = rp.Portfolio(returns=Y)

# Calculating optimum portfolio

# Select method and estimate input parameters:

method_mu='hist' # Method to estimate expected returns based on historical data.
method_cov='hist' # Method to estimate covariance matrix based on historical data.

port.assets_stats(method_mu=method_mu,
                  method_cov=method_cov,
                  )

# Estimate optimal portfolio:

port.solvers = ['MOSEK'] # It is recommended to use mosek when optimizing GMD
port.sol_params = {'MOSEK': {'mosek_params': {mosek.iparam.num_threads: 2}}}

kappa = 0.3
alpha = 0.2
port.kappa = kappa
port.alpha = alpha

model ='Classic' # Could be Classic (historical), BL (Black Litterman) or FM (Factor Model)
rm = 'EDaR' # Risk measure used, this time will be Tail Gini Range
obj = 'Sharpe' # Objective function, could be MinRisk, MaxRet, Utility or Sharpe
hist = True # Use historical scenarios for risk measures that""" ;
    rf:content_hash "20c0d7942f7af3156385a5398eb166ee85ba7610af46882df9354a85a16f15ba" ;
    rf:line_end 5 ;
    rf:line_start 5 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 41 - Mean Relativistic Drawdown at Risk (RLDaR) Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_cell" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 41 - Mean Relativistic Drawdown at Risk (RLDaR) Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2041%20-%20Mean%20Relativistic%20Drawdown%20at%20Risk%20(RLDaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:6> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 6 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """be MinRisk, MaxRet, Utility or Sharpe
hist = True # Use historical scenarios for risk measures that depend on scenarios
rf = 0 # Risk free rate
l = 0 # Risk aversion factor, only useful when obj is 'Utility'

w = port.optimization(model=model, rm=rm, obj=obj, rf=rf, l=l, hist=hist)

display(w.T)""" ;
    rf:content_hash "168eeb7b02169c97346a9de4811163e2bec9e801f8c548b7a24ca98bfaf11552" ;
    rf:line_end 5 ;
    rf:line_start 5 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 41 - Mean Relativistic Drawdown at Risk (RLDaR) Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_cell" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 41 - Mean Relativistic Drawdown at Risk (RLDaR) Optimization.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2041%20-%20Mean%20Relativistic%20Drawdown%20at%20Risk%20(RLDaR)%20Optimization.ipynb::chunk:7> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 7 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content "### 2.2 Plotting portfolio composition" ;
    rf:content_hash "ef90a4ab33afa627ccbd5b0a97736d8dfe8680ce21be268b128bcd780fe0083d" ;
    rf:line_end 6 ;
    rf:line_start 6 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 41 - Mean Relativistic Drawdown at Risk (RLDaR) Optimization.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
