    rf:chunk_index 15 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content """## 3. Estimating Portfolios Using Risk Factors with Other Risk Measures and Stepwise Regression

In this part I will calculate optimal factor risk parity portfolios for several risk measures using the market factors matrix as risk factors.

### 3.1 Calculate Optimal Factor Risk Parity Portfolios based on Market Factors for Several Risk Measures""" ;
    rf:content_hash "b4a2a835ee70e6b6e594927f077810ae3cc3ae40e646b4255f36f27573e5d177" ;
    rf:line_end 14 ;
    rf:line_start 14 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 47 - Risk Parity with Risk Factors.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 47 - Risk Parity with Risk Factors.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2047%20-%20Risk%20Parity%20with%20Risk%20Factors.ipynb::chunk:16> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 16 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """# Risk Measures available:
#
# 'MV': Standard Deviation.
# 'MAD': Mean Absolute Deviation.
# 'MSV': Semi Standard Deviation.
# 'FLPM': First Lower Partial Moment (Omega Ratio).
# 'SLPM': Second Lower Partial Moment (Sortino Ratio).
# 'CVaR': Conditional Value at Risk.
# 'EVaR': Entropic Value at Risk.
# 'WR': Worst Realization (Minimax)
# 'MDD': Maximum Drawdown of uncompounded cumulative returns (Calmar Ratio).
# 'ADD': Average Drawdown of uncompounded cumulative returns.
# 'CDaR': Conditional Drawdown at Risk of uncompounded cumulative returns.
# 'EDaR': Entropic Drawdown at Risk of uncompounded cumulative returns.
# 'UCI': Ulcer Index of uncompounded cumulative returns.

rms = ['MV', 'MAD', 'MSV', 'FLPM', 'SLPM', 'CVaR',
       'EVaR', 'CDaR', 'UCI', 'EDaR']

w_s = pd.DataFrame([])

# When we use hist = True the risk measures all calculated
# using historical returns, while when hist = False the
# risk measures are calculated using the expected returns 
#  based on risk factor model""" ;
    rf:content_hash "0c4500fcb4e8b6d6036bcaa6710a947b567e8acab10dc6fe0f341b7b75d9772e" ;
    rf:line_end 15 ;
    rf:line_start 15 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 47 - Risk Parity with Risk Factors.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_cell" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 47 - Risk Parity with Risk Factors.ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%2047%20-%20Risk%20Parity%20with%20Risk%20Factors.ipynb::chunk:17> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 17 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """= False the
# risk measures are calculated using the expected returns 
#  based on risk factor model: R = a + B * F

for i in rms:
    w = port.rp_optimization(model=model, rm=i, rf=rf, b_f=b_f)
    w_s = pd.concat([w_s, w], axis=1)
    
w_s.columns = rms""" ;
    rf:content_hash "bae5f5518bfa8e0bc1c4069cc7f1a4bcca58f8da862037a89678fb4b3eba0155" ;
    rf:line_end 15 ;
