    rf:chunk_index 13 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content """## 3. Estimating Mean Risk Portfolios with Custom Mean Parameter

In this part I will calculate optimal portfolios for several risk measures using a custom mean parameter as input. First I'm going to calculate the portfolio that maximizes risk adjusted return when CVaR is the risk measure, then I'm going to calculate the portfolios that maximize the risk adjusted return for all available risk measures.

### 3.1 Calculating the portfolio that maximizes Return/CVaR ratio.""" ;
    rf:content_hash "80f325a88d415da92627ac18a185aa2aff00280de2d629318b47cacdfea29dfc" ;
    rf:line_end 12 ;
    rf:line_start 12 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 6 - Portfolio Optimization with Custom Parameters.ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 6 - Portfolio Optimization with Custom Parameters.ipynb" .

