    rf:chunk_index 4 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_section" ;
    rf:content """## 2. Estimating Mean Variance Portfolios with PCR

### 2.1 Estimating the loadings matrix with PCR.

This part is just to visualize how Riskfolio-Lib calculates a loadings matrix using PCR.""" ;
    rf:content_hash "7ec964bcb36c524caad3a690bbbd8924b061c322d006214312c16385d6938d9e" ;
    rf:line_end 4 ;
    rf:line_start 4 ;
    rf:relative_path "Tutorial 9 - Portfolio Optimization using Risk Factors and Principal Components Regression (PCR).ipynb" ;
    rf:section "example_section" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/examples/Tutorial 9 - Portfolio Optimization using Risk Factors and Principal Components Regression (PCR).ipynb" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/Tutorial%209%20-%20Portfolio%20Optimization%20using%20Risk%20Factors%20and%20Principal%20Components%20Regression%20(PCR).ipynb::chunk:5> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 5 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "example_cell" ;
    rf:content """import riskfolio as rp

feature_selection = 'PCR' # Method to select best model, could be PCR or Stepwise
n_components = 0.95 # 95% of explained variance. See PCA in scikit learn for more information

loadings = rp.loadings_matrix(X=X, Y=Y, feature_selection=feature_selection,
                              n_components=n_components)

loadings.style.format("{:.4f}").background_gradient(cmap='RdYlGn')""" ;
    rf:content_hash "3f158ba11976bc47e3f0defacfe728e9c78e3c795952c992edda0dc41f4a7295" ;
