<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/course.rst::chunk:2> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 2 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "section" ;
    rf:content """Motivation
===========

Since its release in March 2nd, 2020; Riskfolio-Lib has become one of the most popular
Portfolio Optimization Python libraries worldwide. However, a large percentage of users
encounter difficulties when using Riskfolio-Lib because they have not had adequate training in
mathematical optimization or mathematical programming.

**It is important to mention that this course helps to fund the continuous development and maintenance
of Riskfolio-Lib due to it is a personal open-source project that is not financed for any institution
like other popular Python projects.**""" ;
    rf:content_hash "9304ca2e3a0f1cf4a5309da108151cb1679e0c8838634857467795bbb0d94424" ;
    rf:line_end 51 ;
    rf:line_start 40 ;
    rf:relative_path "course.rst" ;
    rf:section "Motivation" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/docs/source/course.rst" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/course.rst::chunk:3> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 3 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "section" ;
    rf:content """Objective
===========

The objective of the course is to provide the student with the computational tools that allow them
to design asset allocation strategies using the most modern portfolio optimization techniques that
would be very complicated using a spreadsheet or a traditional programming language.""" ;
    rf:content_hash "7600d855d7062a233082430be732751a351697efb27b958a58c87c8679acb6ce" ;
    rf:line_end 58 ;
    rf:line_start 52 ;
    rf:relative_path "course.rst" ;
    rf:section "Objective" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/docs/source/course.rst" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/course.rst::chunk:4> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 4 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "section" ;
    rf:content """Student Profile
===============

Professionals in the areas of finance, investments, risk management; who wish to improve their
skills in portfolio optimization. It is recommended that the students have basic to intermediate
knowledge of portfolio theory, optimization, calculus, linear algebra and statistics; and intermediate
to advance knowledge of one programming language (Python, R, Julia, Rust, C, C++, VBA, VB.net,
Matlab or similar).""" ;
    rf:content_hash "c47b894e5e234186f4f3ef62df3954ca30f20422f26430fbddda4ea2872af57f" ;
    rf:line_end 67 ;
    rf:line_start 59 ;
    rf:relative_path "course.rst" ;
    rf:section "Student Profile" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/docs/source/course.rst" .

<https://riskfolio-graphrag.io/kg/v2/course.rst::chunk:5> a rf:Chunk ;
    rf:chunk_index 5 ;
    rf:chunk_kind "section" ;
    rf:content """Courses Details
================

* The course will be available, with all materials (recordings, codes, slides and whiteboards), starting **March 28, 2026**.
* The classes are online and asynchronous through our Google Classroom.
* The materials will be updated every two years.""" ;
    rf:content_hash "a3def34de6c3095fed3cd33b0fc18382190a1c30aee116d3d163cf41df981332" ;
    rf:line_end 74 ;
    rf:line_start 68 ;
    rf:relative_path "course.rst" ;
    rf:section "Courses Details" ;
    rf:source_path "/Users/et/Desktop/Data_Projects/Riskfolio-Lib/docs/source/course.rst" .

